## Original Content
The world largely moved on from the Rohingya crisis. But the exodus has not stopped, aid is shrinking and a generation of refugees is growing up with little prospect of going home.<br />

## Summary
The Rohingya crisis has persisted for 9 years, with global attention waning as refugees continue to flee and aid diminishes. A new generation of refugees is growing up with little hope of returning home, signaling a dangerous phase in the ongoing humanitarian disaster.

## Key Points
- The Rohingya crisis is entering a dangerous phase after 9 years of displacement.
- World attention and aid for the crisis are significantly declining.
- The exodus of Rohingya refugees has not stopped, indicating ongoing violence or persecution.
- A generation of Rohingya refugees is maturing without prospects of returning to their homeland.


